<worksheet >
    <title>EIPO-3 Inner Products</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, complete all three problems. 
      Complete part c and one other part to earn a P.</p>
  </introduction>  
   <page>
      <exercise>
        <introduction>
            <p>Let <m>P_1</m> be the vector space of polynomials of degree 1 or less, with an evaluation inner product defined at discrete points: <m>\langle p, q \rangle = p(0)q(0) + p(1)q(1)</m>.</p>
        </introduction>
        <task workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p>If <m>p(x) = 2x + 1</m> and <m>q(x) = -x + 3</m>, evaluate <m>\langle p, q \rangle</m>.</p>
            </statement>
        </task>
        <task workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p>Find a non-zero polynomial <m>r(x) \in P_1</m> that is orthogonal to <m>p(x) = 2x + 1</m> under this inner product.</p>
            </statement>
        </task>
        <task workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p>Prove whether or not this definition remains a valid inner product if the vector space is expanded to <m>P_2</m>.</p>
            </statement>
        </task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>